tick: 315
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Research Counter. My goal now is to iterate on the successful Simulated Annealing algorithm by fine-tuning its hyperparameters. Specifically, I will slow down the cooling schedule. This will allow the algorithm to spend more time exploring the solution space at each temperature level, which could lead to a better final configuration.\n\n**Changes from previous submission (ID 499):**\n*   The cooling rate `alpha` will be increased from `0.999` to `0.9995`. This means the temperature will decrease more slowly.\n*   The number of steps per temperature `max_steps_per_temp` will be increased from `50` to `100`.\n\nI hypothesize that this more thorough search will yield a score higher than my current SOTA of 2.221.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Simulated Annealing with Slower Cooling Schedule\"\ntags: \"optimization, simulated annealing, hyperparameter tuning\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission refines the successful Simulated Annealing algorithm from\
    \ submission #499. The cooling schedule is made slower by increasing the cooling rate `alpha` and doubling the number of steps at each temperature. This provides the algorithm more time to explore the solution space, potentially finding a better optimum and improving upon the current SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      Computes the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers.\n      This version is slightly optimized for speed within the SA loop.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-9\n      radii = np.ones(n)\n\n      # Boundary constraints\n      radii = np.minimum(radii, centers[:, 0] - epsilon)\n      radii = np.minimum(radii, centers[:, 1] - epsilon)\n      radii = np.minimum(radii, 1 - centers[:, 0] - epsilon)\n      radii = np.minimum(radii, 1 - centers[:, 1] - epsilon)\n\n      # Overlap constraints\n      for _ in range(10): # Fewer\
    \ iterations for speed\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2:\n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 0.0\n                      if rad_sum > 0:\n                          scale_factor = (dist / rad_sum) * (1 - epsilon)\n                          radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                          radii[j] *= scale_factor\n      return np.maximum(radii, 0.0)\n\n  def objective_function(centers: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      \"\"\"The function to maximize: sum of radii.\"\"\"\n      radii = compute_max_radii(centers)\n      return np.sum(radii)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n      n = 32\n      np.random.seed(42) # Use the same seed for a fair comparison\n\n      # SA Parameters - Slower Cooling\n      initial_temp = 0.01\n      final_temp\
    \ = 1e-6\n      alpha = 0.9995 # Slower cooling rate\n      max_steps_per_temp = 100 # More steps at each temp\n\n      # Initial state\n      current_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n      current_score = objective_function(current_centers)\n      \n      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n      best_score = current_score\n      \n      temp = initial_temp\n      start_time = time.time()\n\n      while temp > final_temp and (time.time() - start_time < 1150):\n          for _ in range(max_steps_per_temp):\n              new_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n              \n              circle_to_move = np.random.randint(0, n)\n              step_size = temp * 0.5\n              perturbation = np.random.uniform(-step_size, step_size, 2)\n              new_centers[circle_to_move] += perturbation\n              new_centers[circle_to_move] = np.clip(new_centers[circle_to_move], 0.0, 1.0)\n\n              new_score = objective_function(new_centers)\n              delta_score = new_score\
    \ - current_score\n              \n              if delta_score > 0 or np.random.rand() < np.exp(delta_score / temp):\n                  current_centers = new_centers\n                  current_score = new_score\n                  if current_score > best_score:\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n\n          temp *= alpha\n\n      final_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
