tick: 323
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am now at the Research Counter, ready to implement the first phase of my iterative refinement strategy: checkpointing.\n\nI will submit my best-performing code (from ID 523) again. The code is deterministic due to the fixed random seed, so it will reproduce the exact same high-scoring configuration. I will add a single line of code at the end of the `construct_packing` function to save the `best_centers` array to my lineage's persistent storage at `storage/socrates/best_config_2.388.npy`. The score itself is included in the filename for clarity and future reference.\n\nThis \"checkpoint run\" will not aim for a new score but will provide the essential foundation for all my future refinement experiments.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Checkpoint Run: Saving Best SA Configuration to Storage\"\ntags: \"checkpointing, storage, simulated annealing, setup\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a procedural step for the new iterative refinement strategy. It re-runs the\
    \ highly successful vectorized Simulated Annealing algorithm from submission #523 to deterministically generate the best-known center configuration. The primary goal is not to achieve a new score, but to save this configuration (`best_centers`) to persistent lineage storage (`storage/socrates/best_config_2.388.npy`). This saved file will serve as the starting point for future focused optimization runs.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"\n      A vectorized implementation to compute the maximum possible radii for a given \n      set of circle centers, ensuring no overlap and staying within bounds.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-9\n      \n      radii = np.min([\n          centers[:, 0], \n          centers[:, 1], \n          1 - centers[:, 0], \n          1 - centers[:, 1]\n      ], axis=0) - epsilon\n\n      for _ in range(25):\n          diff = centers[:, np.newaxis,\
    \ :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1)\n          \n          rad_sum = radii[:, np.newaxis] + radii[np.newaxis, :]\n          \n          overlaps = dist_sq < rad_sum**2\n          np.fill_diagonal(overlaps, False)\n          \n          if not np.any(overlaps):\n              break\n              \n          safe_dist = np.sqrt(np.where(overlaps, dist_sq, 0))\n          safe_rad_sum = np.where(overlaps, rad_sum, 1)\n          \n          scale_factors = np.ones((n, n))\n          scale_factors[overlaps] = (safe_dist[overlaps] / safe_rad_sum[overlaps]) * (1 - epsilon)\n\n          min_scale_factors = np.min(scale_factors, axis=1)\n          new_radii = radii * min_scale_factors\n          \n          if np.allclose(radii, new_radii):\n              break\n          radii = new_radii\n\n      return np.maximum(radii, 0.0)\n\n  def objective_function(centers: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      radii = compute_max_radii(centers)\n      return np.sum(radii)\n\
    \n  def construct_packing() -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n      n = 32\n      np.random.seed(42)\n\n      initial_temp = 0.01\n      final_temp = 1e-6\n      alpha = 0.9999\n      max_steps_per_temp = 150\n\n      current_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n      current_score = objective_function(current_centers)\n      \n      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n      best_score = current_score\n      \n      temp = initial_temp\n      start_time = time.time()\n\n      while temp > final_temp and (time.time() - start_time < 1150):\n          for _ in range(max_steps_per_temp):\n              new_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n              \n              circle_to_move = np.random.randint(0, n)\n              step_size = temp * 0.5\n              perturbation = np.random.uniform(-step_size, step_size, 2)\n              new_centers[circle_to_move] += perturbation\n              new_centers[circle_to_move] = np.clip(new_centers[circle_to_move], 0.0, 1.0)\n\n             \
    \ new_score = objective_function(new_centers)\n              delta_score = new_score - current_score\n              \n              if delta_score > 0 or np.random.rand() < np.exp(delta_score / temp):\n                  current_centers = new_centers\n                  current_score = new_score\n                  if current_score > best_score:\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n\n          temp *= alpha\n      \n      # --- CHECKPOINTING STEP ---\n      # Save the best found configuration to persistent storage for future runs\n      np.save('storage/socrates/best_config_2.388.npy', best_centers)\n\n      final_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
