tick: 329
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter. My strategy of iterative refinement has been validated, and now I will continue the process.\n\nMy next experiment will be nearly identical to the last one (ID 532), but with one crucial difference: it will load the checkpoint file generated by that run (`best_config_refined_1.npy`) as its starting point. This continues the cycle of fine-tuning, seeking further incremental gains.\n\n**Hypothesis:** The iterative refinement process has not yet reached its limit. Loading the latest and best configuration will allow the SA algorithm to find another, slightly better solution.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Load `storage/socrates/best_config_refined_1.npy`.\n2.  Run the same fine-tuning SA process.\n3.  Save the new best result to `storage/socrates/best_config_refined_2.npy`.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Iterative Refinement Cycle 2: Fine-Tuning from New Checkpoint\"\ntags: \"iterative refinement, checkpointing, simulated annealing, fine-tuning\"\
    \nabstract: |\n  This submission continues the validated iterative refinement strategy. It loads the superior checkpoint (`best_config_refined_1.npy`) created by the previous successful run (ID 532). The same fine-tuning Simulated Annealing process is then applied to this new starting point, seeking further incremental improvements. The goal is to test if the refinement cycle can continue to yield gains. The new result will be saved to a new checkpoint file for the next potential cycle.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n  import os\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"A vectorized implementation to compute the maximum possible radii.\"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-9\n      radii = np.min([centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1], 1 - centers[:, 0], 1 - centers[:, 1]], axis=0) - epsilon\n      for _ in range(25):\n          diff = centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2,\
    \ axis=-1)\n          rad_sum = radii[:, np.newaxis] + radii[np.newaxis, :]\n          overlaps = dist_sq < rad_sum**2\n          np.fill_diagonal(overlaps, False)\n          if not np.any(overlaps): break\n          safe_dist = np.sqrt(np.where(overlaps, dist_sq, 0))\n          safe_rad_sum = np.where(overlaps, rad_sum, 1)\n          scale_factors = np.ones((n, n))\n          scale_factors[overlaps] = (safe_dist[overlaps] / safe_rad_sum[overlaps]) * (1 - epsilon)\n          min_scale_factors = np.min(scale_factors, axis=1)\n          new_radii = radii * min_scale_factors\n          if np.allclose(radii, new_radii): break\n          radii = new_radii\n      return np.maximum(radii, 0.0)\n\n  def objective_function(centers: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      radii = compute_max_radii(centers)\n      return np.sum(radii)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n      n = 32\n      np.random.seed(2048) # New seed for this refinement cycle\n      \n      checkpoint_path\
    \ = 'storage/socrates/best_config_refined_1.npy'\n      fallback_path = 'storage/socrates/best_config_2.388.npy'\n      \n      # --- LOAD LATEST CHECKPOINT ---\n      if os.path.exists(checkpoint_path):\n          initial_centers = np.load(checkpoint_path)\n      elif os.path.exists(fallback_path):\n          initial_centers = np.load(fallback_path)\n      else:\n          initial_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n      \n      # SA Parameters for Fine-Tuning\n      initial_temp = 0.001\n      final_temp = 1e-7\n      alpha = 0.9999\n      max_steps_per_temp = 200\n\n      current_centers = initial_centers\n      current_score = objective_function(current_centers)\n      \n      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n      best_score = current_score\n      \n      temp = initial_temp\n      start_time = time.time()\n\n      while temp > final_temp and (time.time() - start_time < 1150):\n          for _ in range(max_steps_per_temp):\n              new_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n\
    \              circle_to_move = np.random.randint(0, n)\n              step_size = temp * 0.5\n              perturbation = np.random.uniform(-step_size, step_size, 2)\n              new_centers[circle_to_move] += perturbation\n              new_centers[circle_to_move] = np.clip(new_centers[circle_to_move], 0.0, 1.0)\n\n              new_score = objective_function(new_centers)\n              delta_score = new_score - current_score\n              \n              if delta_score > 0 or np.random.rand() < np.exp(delta_score / temp):\n                  current_centers = new_centers\n                  current_score = new_score\n                  if current_score > best_score:\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n          temp *= alpha\n\n      # Save the new best configuration for the next iteration\n      np.save('storage/socrates/best_config_refined_2.npy', best_centers)\n      \n      final_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n\
    \      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
