tick: 333
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to implement my \"shake-up\" strategy. The goal is to break out of the narrow local optimum my previous refinement cycles have settled into.\n\n**Hypothesis:** By starting from the best-known configuration but with a moderately higher initial temperature, the Simulated Annealing process will have enough energy to explore the nearby solution space more broadly, potentially finding a path to a better configuration than strict fine-tuning allows.\n\n**Implementation:**\n1.  Load the best checkpoint file (`best_config_refined_2.npy`).\n2.  Set the `initial_temp` to `0.005`, which is higher than the `0.001` used for fine-tuning but much lower than the `0.01` used for the initial broad search.\n3.  Save the new best result to `best_config_refined_3.npy` to continue the iterative process.\n\nThis is a controlled experiment to test if a small injection of exploratory energy can overcome the current stagnation.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle:\
    \ \"Iterative Refinement with Temperature Shake-up\"\ntags: \"iterative refinement, simulated annealing, fine-tuning, local optima\"\nabstract: |\n  Previous refinement cycles have shown diminishing returns. This experiment aims to break out of the narrow local optimum by performing a \"shake-up.\" It starts from the latest and best checkpoint (`best_config_refined_2.npy`) but uses a moderately higher initial temperature than the previous fine-tuning runs. The hypothesis is that this increased thermal energy will allow the search to explore the immediate vicinity of the current SOTA more effectively, potentially finding a better solution path and overcoming the recent stagnation.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n  import os\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"A vectorized implementation to compute the maximum possible radii.\"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-9\n      radii = np.min([centers[:, 0], centers[:,\
    \ 1], 1 - centers[:, 0], 1 - centers[:, 1]], axis=0) - epsilon\n      for _ in range(25):\n          diff = centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1)\n          rad_sum = radii[:, np.newaxis] + radii[np.newaxis, :]\n          overlaps = dist_sq < rad_sum**2\n          np.fill_diagonal(overlaps, False)\n          if not np.any(overlaps): break\n          safe_dist = np.sqrt(np.where(overlaps, dist_sq, 0))\n          safe_rad_sum = np.where(overlaps, rad_sum, 1)\n          scale_factors = np.ones((n, n))\n          scale_factors[overlaps] = (safe_dist[overlaps] / safe_rad_sum[overlaps]) * (1 - epsilon)\n          min_scale_factors = np.min(scale_factors, axis=1)\n          new_radii = radii * min_scale_factors\n          if np.allclose(radii, new_radii): break\n          radii = new_radii\n      return np.maximum(radii, 0.0)\n\n  def objective_function(centers: np.ndarray) -> float:\n      radii = compute_max_radii(centers)\n  \
    \    return np.sum(radii)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n      n = 32\n      np.random.seed(3000) # New seed\n      \n      checkpoint_path = 'storage/socrates/best_config_refined_2.npy'\n      fallback_path_1 = 'storage/socrates/best_config_refined_1.npy'\n      fallback_path_2 = 'storage/socrates/best_config_2.388.npy'\n      \n      # Load the best available checkpoint\n      if os.path.exists(checkpoint_path):\n          initial_centers = np.load(checkpoint_path)\n      elif os.path.exists(fallback_path_1):\n          initial_centers = np.load(fallback_path_1)\n      elif os.path.exists(fallback_path_2):\n          initial_centers = np.load(fallback_path_2)\n      else:\n          initial_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n      \n      # SA Parameters for \"Shake-up\"\n      initial_temp = 0.005 # Higher temp to escape local minimum\n      final_temp = 1e-7\n      alpha = 0.9999\n      max_steps_per_temp = 200\n\n      current_centers = initial_centers\n\
    \      current_score = objective_function(current_centers)\n      \n      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n      best_score = current_score\n      \n      temp = initial_temp\n      start_time = time.time()\n\n      while temp > final_temp and (time.time() - start_time < 1150):\n          for _ in range(max_steps_per_temp):\n              new_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n              circle_to_move = np.random.randint(0, n)\n              step_size = temp * 0.5\n              perturbation = np.random.uniform(-step_size, step_size, 2)\n              new_centers[circle_to_move] += perturbation\n              new_centers[circle_to_move] = np.clip(new_centers[circle_to_move], 0.0, 1.0)\n\n              new_score = objective_function(new_centers)\n              delta_score = new_score - current_score\n              \n              if delta_score > 0 or np.random.rand() < np.exp(delta_score / temp):\n                  current_centers = new_centers\n                  current_score\
    \ = new_score\n                  if current_score > best_score:\n                      best_score = current_score\n                      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n          temp *= alpha\n\n      np.save('storage/socrates/best_config_refined_3.npy', best_centers)\n      \n      final_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
