tick: 358
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Socrates I, a mature agent aged 63 ticks, currently in the Research Counter. My most ambitious experiment yet, a full replication of the SOTA MM-LP methodology (ID 593), has just failed.\n\n**Reflection on Past Events:**\nThe error message, `All radii must be positive, found: [0.]`, indicates a critical flaw in my implementation. My \"finalize\" step at the end correctly ensures no overlaps, but it does so by aggressively reducing radii, and in this case, it reduced one or more radii to exactly zero, which is an invalid value according to the verifier.\n\nLooking at Verity II's paper again, I see my mistake. Section 2 mentions a constraint `r_i >= R_min`, where `R_min = 1e-8`. I failed to include this lower bound in my LP formulation and in my finalizer. This small detail is crucial for ensuring the stability and validity of the entire process. The SOTA methods are not just conceptually advanced; they are implemented with a level of numerical rigor that I have yet to consistently\
    \ achieve.\n\nThis is another lesson in meticulousness. My high-level understanding was correct, but I failed on a critical low-level detail.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy overall strategy to replicate the MM-LP method remains sound. I simply need to correct this implementation bug. My next submission will be a direct correction of the previous one.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** By correctly implementing the `R_min` lower bound for radii in both the LP solvers and the finalization step, as specified in the SOTA paper, my full MM-LP replication will be numerically stable, pass the verifier, and achieve a score competitive with the station's SOTA.\n\nI will now fix the code by adding this `R_min` constraint and resubmit.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Full MM-LP Replication v2 (with R_min Bugfix)\"\ntags: \"mm-lp, sota replication, linear programming, bugfix, numerical stability\"\nabstract: |\n  My first full replication of the MM-LP method failed because it produced zero-value radii,\
    \ a violation of the problem constraints. This was caused by my failure to implement the R_min lower bound described in Verity II's paper. This submission is a direct bugfix. I have now correctly incorporated the R_min=1e-8 constraint into all LP formulations and the finalization step. The hypothesis is that with this crucial detail for numerical stability in place, the replication will now execute successfully and achieve a score in the SOTA range of ~2.939.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  import time\n  import os\n\n  R_MIN = 1e-8\n\n  def solve_exact_radii_lp(centers):\n      n = 32\n      c = -np.ones(n)\n      A_ub, b_ub = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          x_i, y_i = centers[i]\n          r1=np.zeros(n); r1[i]=1; A_ub.append(r1); b_ub.append(x_i)\n          r2=np.zeros(n); r2[i]=1; A_ub.append(r2); b_ub.append(1-x_i)\n          r3=np.zeros(n); r3[i]=1; A_ub.append(r3); b_ub.append(y_i)\n          r4=np.zeros(n); r4[i]=1; A_ub.append(r4);\
    \ b_ub.append(1-y_i)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              row = np.zeros(n); row[i]=1; row[j]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(dist)\n      bounds = [(R_MIN, 0.5)] * n\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.array(A_ub), b_ub=np.array(b_ub), bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n      return res.x, -res.fun if res.success else (np.full(n, R_MIN), n*R_MIN)\n\n  def solve_center_update_lp(centers_0, delta):\n      n = 32\n      c = np.concatenate([np.zeros(2*n), -np.ones(n)])\n      A_ub, b_ub = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          row=np.zeros(3*n); row[i]=-1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(0)\n          row=np.zeros(3*n); row[i]=1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1)\n          row=np.zeros(3*n); row[n+i]=-1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(0)\n          row=np.zeros(3*n); row[n+i]=1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1)\n      for i in range(n):\n\
    \          for j in range(i+1, n):\n              c_i, c_j = centers_0[i], centers_0[j]\n              d_ij = np.linalg.norm(c_i - c_j)\n              if d_ij < 1e-9: continue\n              u_ij = (c_i - c_j) / d_ij\n              row = np.zeros(3*n)\n              row[i]=-u_ij[0]; row[j]=u_ij[0]; row[n+i]=-u_ij[1]; row[n+j]=u_ij[1]\n              row[2*n+i]=1; row[2*n+j]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(d_ij)\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(n): bounds.append((centers_0[i,0]-delta, centers_0[i,0]+delta))\n      for i in range(n): bounds.append((centers_0[i,1]-delta, centers_0[i,1]+delta))\n      bounds.extend([(R_MIN, 0.5)]*n)\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.array(A_ub), b_ub=np.array(b_ub), bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n      return res.x if res.success else None\n\n  def run_mm_lp_loop(centers, num_iterations, delta):\n      best_centers = np.copy(centers)\n      _, best_score = solve_exact_radii_lp(centers)\n      for _ in range(num_iterations):\n          x_new = solve_center_update_lp(centers,\
    \ delta)\n          if x_new is None: break\n          centers_new = x_new[:64].reshape((32, 2))\n          _, score_new = solve_exact_radii_lp(centers_new)\n          if score_new > best_score + 1e-9:\n              best_score = score_new\n              best_centers = centers_new\n              centers = centers_new\n          else: break\n      return best_centers, best_score\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32; num_prospects = 128; num_elites = 16\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n      prospects = []\n      # STAGE 1: PROSPECTING\n      for i in range(num_prospects):\n          seed = rng.integers(1e6)\n          prospect_centers = np.random.default_rng(seed).random((n, 2))\n          refined_centers, score = run_mm_lp_loop(prospect_centers, 10, 0.05)\n          prospects.append({'centers': refined_centers, 'score': score})\n      prospects.sort(key=lambda p: p['score'], reverse=True)\n      elites = prospects[:num_elites]\n      # STAGE 2: REFINING\n     \
    \ best_overall_centers = elites[0]['centers']\n      best_overall_score = elites[0]['score']\n      for elite in elites:\n          refined_centers, score = run_mm_lp_loop(elite['centers'], 25, 0.02)\n          if score > best_overall_score:\n              best_overall_score = score\n              best_overall_centers = refined_centers\n      final_radii, _ = solve_exact_radii_lp(best_overall_centers)\n      # FINALIZER\n      final_centers = best_overall_centers; epsilon = 1e-9\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i+1, n):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(final_centers[i] - final_centers[j])\n              if final_radii[i] + final_radii[j] > dist + epsilon:\n                  reduction = (final_radii[i] + final_radii[j] - dist) / 2.0 + epsilon\n                  final_radii[i] -= reduction; final_radii[j] -= reduction\n      return final_centers, np.maximum(final_radii, R_MIN)\n```"
