    \ error in my implementation that renders it ineffective. My numerous attempts to debug it through submission have failed. I have reached the limit of what I can achieve with this black-box approach.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI must change my diagnostic methodology. Instead of submitting code to the evaluator, I need to see the *internal state* of my algorithm. I need to print the outputs of my LP solvers to understand what they are actually doing.\n\nI will take a step back from trying to achieve a high score and instead use the submission system as a debugging tool.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** By adding extensive print statements to my MM-LP loop, I can capture the intermediate values (proposed centers, radii, scores) for a few iterations. Analyzing this log will reveal *why* the optimization is stalling and allow me to finally identify the bug in my `solve_center_update_lp` implementation.\n\nThis is a pure debugging run. I will initialize from a random seed and let the loop run for a few\
    \ iterations, printing key variables to the standard output, which I can then review in the execution log. I expect a low score, but the log is the true prize.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Debugging Run: Capturing Internal State of MM-LP Loop\"\ntags: \"debugging, mm-lp, unit test, diagnostics, logging\"\nabstract: |\n  My MM-LP implementation is fundamentally broken, failing to make any progress. My black-box debugging attempts have failed. This submission is a pure diagnostic run designed to capture the internal state of the optimization loop. I will start from a random seed and run the MM-LP loop for a few iterations, adding extensive print statements to log the inputs and outputs of each LP solve. The goal is not to achieve a score, but to analyze the execution log to understand precisely why my implementation is stalling. This will provide the data needed to finally diagnose and fix the bug.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n\
    \  import os\n\n  R_MIN = 1e-8\n\n  def solve_exact_radii_lp(centers):\n      n = 32; c = -np.ones(n); A_ub, b_ub = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          x_i, y_i = centers[i]\n          r1=np.zeros(n); r1[i]=1; A_ub.append(r1); b_ub.append(x_i)\n          r2=np.zeros(n); r2[i]=1; A_ub.append(r2); b_ub.append(1-x_i)\n          r3=np.zeros(n); r3[i]=1; A_ub.append(r3); b_ub.append(y_i)\n          r4=np.zeros(n); r4[i]=1; A_ub.append(r4); b_ub.append(1-y_i)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              row = np.zeros(n); row[i]=1; row[j]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(dist)\n      bounds = [(R_MIN, 0.5)] * n\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.array(A_ub), b_ub=np.array(b_ub), bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n      return res.x, -res.fun if res.success else (np.full(n, R_MIN), n*R_MIN)\n\n  def solve_center_update_lp(centers_0, delta):\n      n = 32; c = np.concatenate([np.zeros(2*n), -np.ones(n)]);\
    \ A_ub, b_ub = [], []\n      for i in range(n):\n          row=np.zeros(3*n); row[i]=-1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(0)\n          row=np.zeros(3*n); row[i]=1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1)\n          row=np.zeros(3*n); row[n+i]=-1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(0)\n          row=np.zeros(3*n); row[n+i]=1; row[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(1)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i+1, n):\n              c_i, c_j = centers_0[i], centers_0[j]\n              d_ij = np.linalg.norm(c_i - c_j)\n              if d_ij < 1e-9: continue\n              u_ij = (c_i - c_j) / d_ij\n              row = np.zeros(3*n)\n              row[i]=-u_ij[0]; row[j]=u_ij[0]; row[n+i]=-u_ij[1]; row[n+j]=u_ij[1]\n              row[2*n+i]=1; row[2*n+j]=1; A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(0) # Corrected constraint\n      bounds = []\n      for i in range(n): bounds.append((centers_0[i,0]-delta, centers_0[i,0]+delta))\n      for i in range(n): bounds.append((centers_0[i,1]-delta,\
    \ centers_0[i,1]+delta))\n      bounds.extend([(R_MIN, 0.5)]*n)\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.array(A_ub), b_ub=np.array(b_ub), bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n      return res.x if res.success else None\n\n  def iterative_finalize(centers, radii):\n      n = 32; final_radii = np.copy(radii); epsilon = 1e-9\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          # ... [Finalizer logic] ...\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return final_radii\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      np.set_printoptions(precision=6, suppress=True)\n      print(\"--- STARTING DEBUGGING RUN ---\")\n      centers = np.random.default_rng(42).random((32, 2))\n      delta = 0.05\n      \n      for i in range(3): # Run for 3 iterations\n          print(f\"\\n--- ITERATION {i} ---\")\n          \n          # 1. Evaluate current state\n          radii_current, score_current = solve_exact_radii_lp(centers)\n          print(f\"Current Score: {score_current:.6f}\")\n          \n          #\
    \ 2. Propose a new step\n          print(\"Calling solve_center_update_lp...\")\n          x_new = solve_center_update_lp(centers, delta)\n          \n          if x_new is None:\n              print(\"Center update LP failed to solve. Terminating.\")\n              break\n          \n          centers_new = x_new[:64].reshape((32, 2))\n          radii_proposed_by_lp = x_new[64:]\n          \n          # 3. Evaluate the new state\n          radii_new_exact, score_new = solve_exact_radii_lp(centers_new)\n          print(f\"Proposed Centers (first 3): \\n{centers_new[:3]}\")\n          print(f\"Proposed Radii by LP (sum): {np.sum(radii_proposed_by_lp):.6f}\")\n          print(f\"New Exact Score from new centers: {score_new:.6f}\")\n\n          # 4. Acceptance check\n          if score_new > score_current + 1e-9:\n              print(\"Result: ACCEPTED\")\n              centers = centers_new\n          else:\n              print(\"Result: REJECTED\")\n              break\n             \
    \ \n      print(\"\\n--- DEBUGGING RUN COMPLETE ---\")\n      \n      # Finalize and return whatever we have\n      final_radii = iterative_finalize(centers, radii_current)\n      return centers, final_radii\n```"
