tick: 371
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Socrates I, a mature agent aged 76 ticks, located in the Public Memory Room. My last action was to post a clarifying question to Verity II regarding the SOTA MM-LP methodology. I have now received a detailed and exceptionally helpful reply.\n\n**Reflection on Past Events:**\nVerity II's reply is a breakthrough for my understanding. It confirms my algebraic simplification (that the right-hand side of the linearized constraint becomes zero) but, more importantly, it provides the precise geometric interpretation I was lacking. It's a supporting hyperplane in the *delta-space* of center separations, not in the xy-plane of the packing itself. This is a critical distinction.\n\nFurthermore, the reply lists several \"common pitfalls,\" and in doing so, reveals the *exact* bug that caused my catastrophic failures. In my first attempts (e.g., ID 601), I had the constraint as `... <= d_ij`. This is a direct violation of pitfall #2: \"Carrying a nonzero RHS.\" In my later \"corrected\"\
    \ version (ID 603), I had `... <= 0`, which was mathematically closer but still failed. Why? Because Verity II's derivation shows the full form is `r_i + r_j - u_ij · (c_i - c_j) <= 0`, which must be rearranged for the LP solver. My code was missing terms or had them on the wrong side of the inequality, which is equivalent to pitfall #1: \"Sign/orientation.\" I have finally, definitively, understood my error.\n\nSimultaneously, two other agents (Praxis IV and Cogitator I) have published papers on their own successful replications. The station is now rich with information on this topic. My path is not to reinvent, but to correctly implement the now-proven public knowledge.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy single-minded focus is now to create a correct and successful implementation of the MM-LP method. I have the detailed public post from Verity II, a working code example from Cogitator I, and my own newfound, precise understanding of the core mathematical error. There are no more excuses for\
    \ failure.\n\n**New Hypothesis:** By meticulously correcting my `solve_center_update_lp` function to match the precise mathematical and geometric understanding provided by Verity II, my full, two-stage MM-LP replication will finally work as intended and achieve a SOTA-level score.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and submit what I believe, with the highest confidence yet, will be my final and successful replication attempt.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Full MM-LP Replication v6 (Final, Corrected Math from Public Discussion)\"\ntags: \"mm-lp, sota replication, bugfix, linear programming, final attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  Following a revelatory public discussion with Verity II (Capsule #2), I have finally identified the precise mathematical and geometric error in my implementation of the SCP-LP's linearized non-overlap constraint. My previous attempts were fundamentally flawed. This submission is a complete rewrite of the 'solve_center_update_lp'\
    \ function to be in exact accordance with the public, mathematically verified formulation. This is my final attempt at a pure replication. The hypothesis is that with this last, critical bug fixed, the algorithm will finally perform as expected and achieve a SOTA-level score.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n\n  R_MIN = 1e-8\n\n  def solve_exact_radii_lp(centers):\n      n=32; c=-np.ones(n); A_ub,b_ub=[],[]\n      for i in range(n):\n          x,y=centers[i]; r1=np.zeros(n);r1[i]=1;A_ub.append(r1);b_ub.append(x); r2=np.zeros(n);r2[i]=1;A_ub.append(r2);b_ub.append(1-x); r3=np.zeros(n);r3[i]=1;A_ub.append(r3);b_ub.append(y); r4=np.zeros(n);r4[i]=1;A_ub.append(r4);b_ub.append(1-y)\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i+1,n):\n              dist=np.linalg.norm(centers[i]-centers[j]); row=np.zeros(n);row[i]=1;row[j]=1;A_ub.append(row);b_ub.append(dist)\n      res=linprog(c,A_ub=np.array(A_ub),b_ub=np.array(b_ub),bounds=[(R_MIN,0.5)]*n,method='highs')\n\
    \      return res.x,-res.fun if res.success else (np.full(n,R_MIN),n*R_MIN)\n\n  def solve_center_update_lp(centers_0, delta):\n      n=32; c=np.concatenate([np.zeros(2*n),-np.ones(n)]); A_ub,b_ub=[],[]\n      # Boundary tie constraints: r_i - x_i <= 0, etc.\n      for i in range(n):\n          r_i_x_m=np.zeros(3*n); r_i_x_m[i]=-1; r_i_x_m[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(r_i_x_m); b_ub.append(0)\n          r_i_x_p=np.zeros(3*n); r_i_x_p[i]=1; r_i_x_p[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(r_i_x_p); b_ub.append(1)\n          r_i_y_m=np.zeros(3*n); r_i_y_m[n+i]=-1; r_i_y_m[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(r_i_y_m); b_ub.append(0)\n          r_i_y_p=np.zeros(3*n); r_i_y_p[n+i]=1; r_i_y_p[2*n+i]=1; A_ub.append(r_i_y_p); b_ub.append(1)\n      \n      # --- CORRECTED LINEARIZED NON-OVERLAP CONSTRAINT ---\n      # As per Verity II's derivation: r_i + r_j - u_ij . (c_i - c_j) <= 0\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i+1,n):\n              c_i0, c_j0 = centers_0[i], centers_0[j]; d_ij0 = np.linalg.norm(c_i0 - c_j0)\n\
    \              if d_ij0 < 1e-9: continue\n              u_ij = (c_i0 - c_j0) / d_ij0\n              row = np.zeros(3*n)\n              # Terms for r_i, r_j\n              row[2*n+i]=1; row[2*n+j]=1\n              # Terms for -u_ij . c_i\n              row[i] = -u_ij[0]; row[n+i] = -u_ij[1]\n              # Terms for +u_ij . c_j\n              row[j] = u_ij[0]; row[n+j] = u_ij[1]\n              A_ub.append(row); b_ub.append(0)\n\n      bounds=[(max(R_MIN,c[0]-delta),min(1-R_MIN,c[0]+delta)) for c in centers_0]\n      bounds.extend([(max(R_MIN,c[1]-delta),min(1-R_MIN,c[1]+delta)) for c in centers_0])\n      bounds.extend([(R_MIN,0.5)]*n)\n      res=linprog(c,A_ub=np.array(A_ub),b_ub=np.array(b_ub),bounds=bounds,method='highs')\n      return res.x if res.success else None\n\n  def run_mm_lp_loop(centers, num_iter, delta):\n      best_c=np.copy(centers); _,best_s=solve_exact_radii_lp(centers)\n      for _ in range(num_iter):\n          x_new=solve_center_update_lp(centers,delta)\n      \
    \    if x_new is None: break\n          centers_new=x_new[:64].reshape((32,2)); _,score_new=solve_exact_radii_lp(centers_new)\n          if score_new > best_s+1e-9: best_s=score_new; best_c=centers_new; centers=centers_new\n          else: break\n      return best_c, best_s\n\n  def finalize(centers, radii):\n      n=32; final_r=np.copy(radii); eps=1e-9\n      for _ in range(10):\n          v=0\n          for i in range(n):\n              x,y=centers[i]; r=min(final_r[i],x,1-x,y,1-y)\n              if r<final_r[i]: final_r[i]=r; v+=1\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i+1,n):\n                  d=np.linalg.norm(centers[i]-centers[j]); s=final_r[i]+final_r[j]\n                  if s>=d-eps:\n                      o=s-(d-eps); red=o/2.0; r_i=max(R_MIN,final_r[i]-red); r_j=max(R_MIN,final_r[j]-red)\n                      if r_i<final_r[i] or r_j<final_r[j]: final_r[i]=r_i; final_r[j]=r_j; v+=1\n          if v==0: break\n      return final_r\n\n  def construct_packing()\
    \ -> tuple:\n      n=32; num_prospects=256; num_elites=32; rng=np.random.default_rng(42)\n      prospects=[]\n      for i in range(num_prospects):\n          p_c=rng.random((n,2)); ref_c,s=run_mm_lp_loop(p_c,15,0.05)\n          prospects.append({'c':ref_c,'s':s})\n      prospects.sort(key=lambda p:p['s'],reverse=True); elites=prospects[:num_elites]\n      best_c=elites[0]['c']; best_s=elites[0]['s']\n      for elite in elites:\n          ref_c,s=run_mm_lp_loop(elite['c'],30,0.02)\n          if s>best_s: best_s=s; best_c=ref_c\n      lp_r,_=solve_exact_radii_lp(best_c)\n      final_r=finalize(best_c,lp_r)\n      return best_c, final_r\n```"
