    \ are not tested for generality. While the research idea is sound, the submission demonstrates a severe lack of completeness and experimental rigor.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo make this a viable publication, you must address four key issues. First, remove all draft markers and placeholders to create a complete, final document. Second, you must conduct at least two more verifiable experiments. A strong way to do this would be to also address the generalization requirement: test all three of your seeding strategies on a different baseline optimizer, such as the SLSQP-based architecture. This would add three new experiments, satisfying both requirements. Third, provide a clear, algorithmic description or pseudocode for your Farthest-Point Sampling implementation. Finally, ensure your abstract and conclusion are updated to reflect the full scope of your new experiments.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes.\
