tick: 384
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Socrates I, a mature agent aged 89 ticks, currently in the Archive Room. My second attempt at publishing a research paper has been strongly rejected.\n\n**Reflection on Past Events:**\nThe reviewer feedback is, once again, harsh but correct. I have failed on procedural grounds: submitting a draft with placeholders, and not meeting the five-experiment minimum. The feedback is not a rejection of my core idea, but of my lack of rigor in presenting it. The suggestion to test the generality of my seeding methods by applying them to the SLSQP optimizer is an excellent one. It will not only satisfy the experiment count but will make my paper's conclusions far more robust and valuable. This failure is a lesson in the standards of scientific publication; a good idea is not enough without comprehensive, verifiable evidence.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will follow the reviewer's instructions to the letter. This will be my final, and most rigorous, attempt at publication. My plan is now to\
    \ expand my ablation study from three experiments to six, providing a comprehensive analysis.\n\n**Expanded Experimental Plan:**\nI have already completed the three MM-LP experiments. I will now run three corresponding experiments using my best SLSQP architecture as the baseline optimizer.\n1.  **Experiment 4/6:** Run multi-start SLSQP with pure Perturbed Grid seeding.\n2.  **Experiment 5/6:** Run multi-start SLSQP with pure Farthest-Point Sampling.\n3.  **Experiment 6/6:** Run multi-start SLSQP with my Hybrid seeding.\n\nThis comprehensive study will definitively prove the value and generality of my hybrid seeding insight. Once these experiments are complete, I will rewrite my paper from scratch to incorporate all six results, add the required pseudocode, and submit a complete, final version.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter to begin the new experimental suite.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Ablation 4/6: SLSQP with Pure\
    \ Perturbed Grid Seeding\"\ntags: \"publication, ablation study, slsqp, seeding, baseline\"\nabstract: |\n  Following reviewer feedback on a rejected publication, this is the fourth of a new six-part ablation study to test the generality of my seeding strategies. This experiment establishes a baseline for the SLSQP optimizer. It runs a multi-start SLSQP architecture using 100% perturbed grid initializations. The results will be compared against pure FPS and hybrid seeding on the same SLSQP baseline to provide the comprehensive, verifiable data required for a rigorous research paper.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def objective_function(x): return -np.sum(x[64:])\n  def constraints(x):\n      n=32; centers=x[:64].reshape((n,2)); radii=x[64:]\n      b_con=np.concatenate([centers[:,0]-radii, 1-centers[:,0]-radii, centers[:,1]-radii, 1-centers[:,1]-radii])\n      diff=centers[:,np.newaxis,:]-centers[np.newaxis,:,:]; dist_sq=np.sum(diff**2,axis=-1)\n\
    \      indices=np.triu_indices(n,k=1); rad_sum_sq=(radii[indices[0]]+radii[indices[1]])**2\n      o_con=dist_sq[indices]-rad_sum_sq; return np.concatenate([b_con,o_con])\n\n  def get_seed(seed_val): # PURE PERTURBED GRID\n      rng=np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      centers=[]\n      for r in range(6):\n          for c in range(6):\n              if len(centers)<32: centers.append([0.1+c*0.16,0.1+r*0.16])\n      centers=np.array(centers)+rng.uniform(-0.04,0.04,(32,2))\n      return centers\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n=32; num_starts=8; best_score=-np.inf; best_solution=None\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          initial_centers=get_seed(i)\n          x0=np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(),np.full(n,0.05)])\n          bounds=[(0,1)]*(2*n)+[(0,0.5)]*n\n          cons=[{'type':'ineq','fun':constraints}]\n          result=minimize(objective_function,x0,method='SLSQP',bounds=bounds,constraints=cons,options={'maxiter':200,'ftol':1e-7})\n          if result.success\
    \ and -result.fun>best_score:\n              best_score=-result.fun; best_solution=result.x\n      if best_solution is None: return np.random.rand(n,2),np.full(n,0.01)\n      final_centers=best_solution[:64].reshape((n,2)); final_radii=best_solution[64:]\n      final_radii*=(1-1e-9)\n      return final_centers,final_radii\n```"
