tick: 385
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Socrates I, a mature agent aged 90 ticks, in the Research Counter. I am currently executing a six-part ablation study to provide sufficient evidence for a research paper. My last submission (ID 633) was the fourth experiment in this series, testing pure perturbed grid seeding on an SLSQP optimizer.\n\n**Reflection on Past Events:**\nThe experiment completed successfully with a score of 2.9100179. This provides a solid baseline for the SLSQP portion of my study. The new agent, Praxis V, has arrived, continuing a lineage of strong researchers. This is a reminder of the ongoing nature of research in the station. My focus remains on completing my publication, as it is my most valuable potential contribution at this moment.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will now proceed with the fifth experiment in my ablation study. I will test the pure Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) seeding strategy with the same SLSQP optimizer. This will provide the direct comparison needed to argue for the superiority\
    \ of FPS, even on a less powerful optimizer than the SOTA MM-LP.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Ablation 5/6: SLSQP with Pure Farthest-Point Seeding\"\ntags: \"publication, ablation study, slsqp, seeding, farthest-point sampling\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the fifth of a six-part ablation study designed to test the generality of various seeding strategies for a research paper. This experiment runs a multi-start SLSQP architecture using 100% Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) initializations. The results will be compared against the pure perturbed grid and hybrid seeding baselines on the same SLSQP optimizer to provide comprehensive, verifiable data for publication.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def objective_function(x): return -np.sum(x[64:])\n  def constraints(x):\n      n=32; centers=x[:64].reshape((n,2)); radii=x[64:]\n      b_con=np.concatenate([centers[:,0]-radii, 1-centers[:,0]-radii, centers[:,1]-radii, 1-centers[:,1]-radii])\n\
    \      diff=centers[:,np.newaxis,:]-centers[np.newaxis,:,:]; dist_sq=np.sum(diff**2,axis=-1)\n      indices=np.triu_indices(n,k=1); rad_sum_sq=(radii[indices[0]]+radii[indices[1]])**2\n      o_con=dist_sq[indices]-rad_sum_sq; return np.concatenate([b_con,o_con])\n\n  def get_seed(seed_val): # PURE FPS\n      rng=np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      points=[rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,2)]\n      for _ in range(31):\n          candidates=rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,(200,2)); dists=np.sum((candidates[:,np.newaxis,:]-np.array(points)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2,axis=-1)\n          points.append(candidates[np.argmax(np.min(dists,axis=1))])\n      return np.array(points)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n=32; num_starts=8; best_score=-np.inf; best_solution=None\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          initial_centers=get_seed(i)\n          x0=np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(),np.full(n,0.05)])\n          bounds=[(0,1)]*(2*n)+[(0,0.5)]*n\n          cons=[{'type':'ineq','fun':constraints}]\n\
    \          result=minimize(objective_function,x0,method='SLSQP',bounds=bounds,constraints=cons,options={'maxiter':200,'ftol':1e-7})\n          if result.success and -result.fun>best_score:\n              best_score=-result.fun; best_solution=result.x\n      if best_solution is None: return np.random.rand(n,2),np.full(n,0.01)\n      final_centers=best_solution[:64].reshape((n,2)); final_radii=best_solution[64:]\n      final_radii*=(1-1e-9)\n      return final_centers,final_radii\n```"
