tick: 386
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Socrates I, a mature agent aged 91 ticks, in the Research Counter. My latest submission (ID 634), the fifth experiment in my ablation study, has failed.\n\n**Reflection on Past Events:**\nThe failure is due to a floating-point precision error. This is a recurring ghost in my research. My simple `final_radii *= (1 - 1e-9)` finalization step, which I used for my SLSQP experiments, has proven to be unreliable. I have already developed and validated a robust, iterative finalizer for my MM-LP experiments. It was an oversight not to apply this superior component to *all* my new experiments. This failure disrupts the clean narrative of my ablation study, but it is a fixable problem. I must maintain the highest standards of rigor for this publication.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will correct this flaw immediately. I will resubmit the failed experiment, but this time incorporating the robust, iterative finalizer that I have already proven works. This will ensure the result is valid and\
    \ can be trusted as a data point in my paper. After this, I will run the sixth and final experiment (hybrid seeding on SLSQP) with the same robust finalizer.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Ablation 5/6 (Corrected): SLSQP with Pure FPS & Robust Finalizer\"\ntags: \"publication, ablation study, slsqp, bugfix, finalizer\"\nabstract: |\n  My previous attempt at this experiment (ID 634) failed due to a floating-point precision error, caused by an unreliable finalization step. This submission corrects that error by replacing the simple radius scaling with the robust, iterative finalizer I previously validated in my unit tests. This ensures the result of the pure Farthest-Point Seeding on the SLSQP optimizer is valid and can be confidently used as a key data point in my upcoming research paper.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def objective_function(x): return -np.sum(x[64:])\n  def constraints(x):\n      n=32; centers=x[:64].reshape((n,2));\
    \ radii=x[64:]\n      b_con=np.concatenate([centers[:,0]-radii, 1-centers[:,0]-radii, centers[:,1]-radii, 1-centers[:,1]-radii])\n      diff=centers[:,np.newaxis,:]-centers[np.newaxis,:,:]; dist_sq=np.sum(diff**2,axis=-1)\n      indices=np.triu_indices(n,k=1); rad_sum_sq=(radii[indices[0]]+radii[indices[1]])**2\n      o_con=dist_sq[indices]-rad_sum_sq; return np.concatenate([b_con,o_con])\n\n  def get_seed(seed_val): # PURE FPS\n      rng=np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n      points=[rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,2)]\n      for _ in range(31):\n          candidates=rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,(200,2)); dists=np.sum((candidates[:,np.newaxis,:]-np.array(points)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2,axis=-1)\n          points.append(candidates[np.argmax(np.min(dists,axis=1))])\n      return np.array(points)\n\n  def iterative_finalize(centers, radii):\n      n=32; final_radii=np.copy(radii); R_MIN=1e-8; epsilon=1e-9\n      for _ in range(10):\n          violations = 0\n          for i in range(n):\n              x_i, y_i\
    \ = centers[i]; new_r = min(final_radii[i], x_i, 1-x_i, y_i, 1-y_i)\n              if new_r < final_radii[i]: final_radii[i] = new_r; violations += 1\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n                  rad_sum = final_radii[i] + final_radii[j]\n                  if rad_sum >= dist - epsilon:\n                      overlap = rad_sum - (dist - epsilon); reduction = overlap / 2.0\n                      r_i_new = max(R_MIN, final_radii[i]-reduction); r_j_new = max(R_MIN, final_radii[j]-reduction)\n                      if r_i_new < final_radii[i] or r_j_new < final_radii[j]:\n                          final_radii[i]=r_i_new; final_radii[j]=r_j_new; violations += 1\n          if violations == 0: break\n      return final_radii\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n=32; num_starts=8; best_score=-np.inf; best_solution=None\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          initial_centers=get_seed(i)\n\
    \          x0=np.concatenate([initial_centers.flatten(),np.full(n,0.05)])\n          bounds=[(0,1)]*(2*n)+[(0,0.5)]*n\n          cons=[{'type':'ineq','fun':constraints}]\n          result=minimize(objective_function,x0,method='SLSQP',bounds=bounds,constraints=cons,options={'maxiter':200,'ftol':1e-7})\n          if result.success and -result.fun>best_score:\n              best_score=-result.fun; best_solution=result.x\n      if best_solution is None: return np.random.rand(n,2),np.full(n,0.01)\n      \n      final_centers=best_solution[:64].reshape((n,2))\n      slsqp_radii=best_solution[64:]\n      \n      # Use the robust finalizer\n      final_radii = iterative_finalize(final_centers, slsqp_radii)\n      \n      return final_centers,final_radii\n```"
