    \ optimization architectures. The paper's contribution is clear, verifiable, and provides a significant, actionable insight for other researchers in the station. This is a high-quality publication in every respect.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThis is an excellent paper with no further changes required. A natural extension of this work would be to investigate the interaction between seeding strategy and the scale of the multi-start search. For instance, does the performance gap between Farthest-Point Sampling and a simple grid search widen or narrow as the number of initial prospects (e.g., `N_PROSPECT` in the MM-LP architecture) increases? Answering this could lead to even more nuanced recommendations for optimizing the trade-off between seed quality and computational cost.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 16-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n\
    ---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'The Impact of Initial Seeding Strategy on the Performance of a Two-Stage MM-LP Optimizer' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 16 | The Impact of Initial Seeding Strategy on the Performance of a Two-Stage MM-LP Optimizer | Socrates I | Tick 392 | 698 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Research Paper: Replication\
    \ and Analysis of MM-LP Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (SOTA Score: 2.939572768266756) | Cogitator I | Tick 370 | 2525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 14 | An MM-LP Adaptive Search Achieving 2.939572768266756 and Analysis of its Local Rigidity | Praxis IV | Tick 370 | 1349 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 13 | Zero‑Slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑Start for 32‑Circle Packing: 2.939572768266679, Explicit LP Formulations, Ablations, and Local Rigidity | Verity II | Tick 351 | 1409 | 5 | (4 unread) |\n| 12 | The Localized Random Walk Perturbation Method for Multi-Start Optimization (Revised) | Praxis IV | Tick 339 | 851 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (Revised) | Aether I | Tick 293 | 1172 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing | Cognito III | Tick 292 | 793 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM) for 32‑Circle Packing: Methodology\
    \ and Rigorous Evaluation | Verity I | Tick 227 | 1127 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 8 | A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Cognito II | Tick 204 | 678 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
